#
# Conformance case: derivation/org-membership-propagation
#
# AC: a cross-slice derivation rule's head appears in the native materialization.
#
# input.nq models a two-level organizational nest as DATA: alice gmeow:memberOf a finance
# department that is gmeow:subOrganizationOf a company that is gmeow:subOrganizationOf a
# holding company. The rule is recursive on gmeow:memberOf, so it climbs the whole nest.
#
# The rule under test — a monotone positive-Horn logic:Rule mirroring the production
# logic:ruleOrgMembershipPropagation (gmeow:memberOf ∘ gmeow:subOrganizationOf ⇒
# gmeow:memberOf). Because gmeow:memberOf occurs in both head and body, the least-fixpoint
# chase propagates membership up an arbitrarily deep nest: materialized.nq is a strict
# superset of input.nq carrying the derived memberships all the way to the holding company
# — proof the recursive propagation materializes (logic:ExactPreservation). This is the
# native-chase form of the same propagation the gmeow:memberOf owl:propertyChainAxiom
# expresses for the OWL 2 RL closure.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/derivation/org-membership-propagation/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# gmeow:memberOf(agent, org) ∧ gmeow:subOrganizationOf(org, parent)
#   ⇒ gmeow:memberOf(agent, parent)
ex:ruleOrgMembershipPropagation
    a logic:Rule ;
    logic:provenance ex:ruleOrgMembershipPropagation ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?agent" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:memberOf ;
        rdf:object    "?parent"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?agent" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:memberOf ;
        rdf:object    "?org"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?org" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:subOrganizationOf ;
        rdf:object    "?parent"
    ] .
